From: Tyler Baker <tyler@baker.engineering>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_hid: drop full-speed bInterval to 1 ms

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [system-specific tuning]

f_hid.c hardcodes bInterval = 10 on the full-speed interrupt endpoints,
so a configfs HID gadget on a FS-only controller (the AM335x MUSB on
this board) is polled at 100 Hz. That is a conservative default for a
generic HID device — a typical keyboard does not benefit from anything
faster — but for input devices whose value lies in the cadence (gaming
mice and controllers) the host-side poll rate is itself a fingerprint:
every modern retail gaming mouse polls at 1000 Hz, and a 100 Hz device
is trivially identifiable as "not a real gaming mouse" by any code
that reads the endpoint descriptor.

This board is a dedicated HID-passthrough appliance whose entire
purpose is to forward gaming input. Drop bInterval to 1 (1 ms = 1000
Hz) on both FS interrupt endpoints. USB bandwidth is not a constraint:
1000 Hz x (8 byte keyboard report + 4 byte mouse report) = 12 KB/s on
a 12 Mbps bus, well under 1% utilisation. The gadget only emits a
report when there is new input to send, so the host simply NAKs on
empty polls — the change raises the cadence ceiling, it does not
force a fixed packet rate.

The upstream FIXME above each endpoint descriptor asks for this to
become a configfs attribute. Until that lands in mainline this is a
two-line tree-local change that matches what this layer needs.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler@baker.engineering>
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
@@ -233,7 +233,7 @@ static struct usb_endpoint_descriptor hidg_fs_in_ep_desc = {
 	.bEndpointAddress	= USB_DIR_IN,
 	.bmAttributes		= USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_INT,
 	/*.wMaxPacketSize	= DYNAMIC */
-	.bInterval		= 10, /* FIXME: Add this field in the
+	.bInterval		= 1,  /* FIXME: Add this field in the
 				       * HID gadget configuration?
 				       * (struct hidg_func_descriptor)
 				       */
@@ -245,7 +245,7 @@ static struct usb_endpoint_descriptor hidg_fs_out_ep_desc = {
 	.bEndpointAddress	= USB_DIR_OUT,
 	.bmAttributes		= USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_INT,
 	/*.wMaxPacketSize	= DYNAMIC */
-	.bInterval		= 10, /* FIXME: Add this field in the
+	.bInterval		= 1,  /* FIXME: Add this field in the
 				       * HID gadget configuration?
 				       * (struct hidg_func_descriptor)
 				       */
